<title>USA: Ontrak transfers Teleparts unit.</title>
<headline>Ontrak transfers Teleparts unit.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>OnTrak Systems Inc said Wednesday it had split off Teleparts International Inc to Kenneth Smith, OnTrak's founder and former chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Teleparts was a wholly-owned subsidiary selling spare parts to the semiconductor industry.  OnTrak transferred its Teleparts stock to Smith in exchange for shares of OnTrak common stock, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said it intends to focus on its core business of supplying advanced wafer processing equipment to the semiconductor industry.</p>
<p>The company said revenues from Teleparts do not constitute a material portion of OnTrak's consolidated revenues.</p>
